      "id": "2507.14910v1",
      "title": "Through the Looking Glass: Bitcoin Treasury Companies",
      "authors": [
        "B K Meister"
      ],
      "abstract": "Bitcoin treasury companies have taken stock markets by storm amassing\nbillions of dollars worth of tokens. More than a hundred companies active in\nvarious crypto-tokens, not just Bitcoin, are listed. The ability to generate\nleverage, for example stemming from borrowing collateralized by stock\nportfolios, helps to understand this phenomenon.\n  In addition, the extension of the binary-choice Kelly criterion to\nincorporate uncertainty in the form of the Kullback-Leibler divergence or more\ngenerally Bregman divergence is studied.",
      "categories": [
        "q-fin.PM"
      ],
